method.description:
Calls this script function with positional arguments from [param args], converting them from Godot values. A [PuertsScriptValue] argument must be valid and belong to the same environment. The script global object is passed as the receiver; use [method call_method] for an object's method.
			Returns a result wrapper, or [code]null[/code] if the value is not callable, argument conversion fails, or the script throws an exception.
			For an initialized ECMAScript [code]environment[/code]:
			[codeblocks]
			[gdscript]
			var function := environment.eval("(a, b) => a + b")
			if function != null:
			    var result: PuertsScriptValue = function.call([20, 22])
			    if result != null:
			        print(result.to_native()) # 42
			[/gdscript]
			[/codeblocks]
